nt-issued photo ID and record full name, email, and phone number before account creation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-018\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"remain held indefinitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-011\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires reserved items on the pickup shelf to be held indefinitely until cancelled by the Member, conflicting with SD-011 which automatically cancels uncollected holds after 72 hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses multiple 'and/or' coordinators, leaving unclear which combination of actions is required or what conditions determine each action.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without specifying which actor (e.g., Librarian, Administrator, or Billing Service) reviews, approves, and logs fine waiver requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the discretionary weak phrase 'if appropriate' without defining the criteria for dispatching alerts (and omits how long before the due date they should be sent).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved TBD placeholder for the payment receipt retention period.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap on accumulated fines\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies an overdue fine of $1.25 USD per day with no cap, conflicting with SD-019's rate of $0.50 USD per day capped at $20.00 USD per item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-020\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Permits renewing items regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance, conflicting with SD-020 which blocks renewals when unpaid fines exceed $5.00 USD.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"each Patron's active loan count and enforce the 5-item borrowing limit on the Patron profile screen\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-009\",\n        \"SD-015\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the undefined term 'Patron' instead of 'Member' (used in SD-009 and throughout the specification), and enforces a 5-item limit matching SD-009 while conflicting with SD-015's 8-item limit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"quickly even when many users are querying the catalog simultaneously\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms 'quickly' and 'many users' without specifying response-time or concurrency thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the weak phrase 'where possible', leaving the conditions under which term highlighting is required undefined.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient ISBN matching accuracy and acceptable response times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective, unquantified terms 'sufficient' and 'acceptable' without measurable accuracy or latency targets.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently process large batch MARC21 files without noticeable system slowdown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague terms 'efficiently', 'large', and 'noticeable system slowdown' without defining file sizes, throughput, or performance impact limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States that the Catalog Service shall detect active loans or holds on deletion attempts, but omits the resulting action (e.g., blocking deletion and returning an error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved TBD placeholder for the database backup execution interval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important administrative actions in a timely manner and retain them for an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms 'important', 'in a timely manner', and 'appropriate period' without specifying which actions, logging latency, or retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Failover Manager shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Only specifies logging FAILOVER-01 when the primary database node is unreachable for over 10 seconds, omitting the actual failover or recovery action.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate transport security and clear error messages\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective terms 'adequate' and 'clear' without specifying concrete transport security standards or error message requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"accept any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Accepts any password of at least 8 characters, conflicting with SD-002's minimum of 12 characters with uppercase, lowercase, and numeric complexity rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Keeps web portal sessions active for 60 minutes of inactivity, conflicting with SD-004's 15-minute inactivity timeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so